## ⚡ Quick Start

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The first run will download the Mistral model (~7 GB). Subsequent starts are near-instant.

### 🐧 Linux & 🍎 macOS
```bash
git clone [https://github.com/oleszyk-ai/parse-local.git](https://github.com/oleszyk-ai/parse-local.git)
cd parse-local
chmod +x setup.sh && ./setup.sh
source .venv/bin/activate && python -m app.main
```

### 🪟 Windows
```powershell
git clone [https://github.com/oleszyk-ai/parse-local.git](https://github.com/oleszyk-ai/parse-local.git)
cd parse-local
./setup.bat
.venv\Scripts\activate
python -m app.main
```

### 🐳 Docker
```bash
docker-compose up --build
```

Once running, open your browser to **[http://localhost:8000](http://localhost:8000)**

---

## 📋 Requirements

| Resource | Minimum | Recommended |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Python** | 3.10+ | 3.11+ |
| **RAM** | 8 GB | 16 GB+ |
| **Disk** | 8 GB free | NVMe SSD |
| **GPU** | Optional | NVIDIA 8GB+ VRAM |

---

## 🔌 API Reference

### Scrape a live URL
`POST /api/scrape/url`
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/scrape/url \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "url": "[https://news.ycombinator.com](https://news.ycombinator.com)",
    "prompt": "Extract the top 10 story titles and scores"
  }'
```

### Parse raw HTML
`POST /api/scrape/html`
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/scrape/html \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "html": "<div><h1>Product A</h1><span>$20</span></div>",
    "prompt": "Extract all product names and prices"
  }'
```

---

## ⚙️ Configuration

Create a `.env` file in the project root to customize performance:

```ini
N_GPU_LAYERS=-1     # -1 = all layers on GPU, 0 = CPU only
N_CTX=8192          # Context window (increase for larger pages)
TEMPERATURE=0.1     # Lower = more consistent JSON
PORT=8000           # Server port
```

---

## 🖥️ GPU Acceleration

> [!TIP]
> Using a GPU makes extraction 5–10x faster.

**NVIDIA (CUDA)**
```bash
pip uninstall llama-cpp-python -y
CMAKE_ARGS="-DGGML_CUDA=on" pip install llama-cpp-python --no-cache-dir
```

**Apple Silicon (Metal)**
```bash
pip uninstall llama-cpp-python -y
CMAKE_ARGS="-DGGML_METAL=on" pip install llama-cpp-python --no-cache-dir
```

---

## 🔧 Troubleshooting

<details>
<summary><b>Model download failed</b></summary>
Download <code>Mistral-Nemo-Instruct-2407-Q4_K_M.gguf</code> manually from 
<a href="https://huggingface.co/bartowski/Mistral-Nemo-Instruct-2407-GGUF">bartowski/Mistral-Nemo-Instruct-2407-GGUF</a> 
and place it in the <code>models/</code> directory.
</details>

<details>
<summary><b>llama-cpp-python install failed</b></summary>
Ensure build tools are installed:
<br>
<b>Linux:</b> <code>sudo apt-get install build-essential cmake -y</code><br>
<b>macOS:</b> <code>xcode-select --install</code><br>
<b>Windows:</b> Install <a href="https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/visual-cpp-build-tools/">VS Build Tools</a> with "C++ build tools" selected.
</details>

